course: dictionary
lesson: 13684
title: Initiation: starting and joining in
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An initiation is the start of something, or a welcome into a group. The word comes from the verb initiate, which means to begin something or to admit someone as a new member. Look at the words around it to find the meaning. «The club's initiation was a secret password and a handshake.» The clues are club, password and handshake, so initiation must mean a ceremony that makes you a new member.
explain: Initiation can also mean a first try at something new. «Her initiation into cooking was making toast, and it burnt.» The word into tells you it is a first step into a new activity. Check by swapping in your meaning: "her start into cooking" still makes sense, so you are right.
explain: Be careful, because some initiations are cruel. «The bully called it an initiation, but the tests were cruel and unsafe.» Schools and clubs ban this kind of hazing, because a welcome should never hurt anyone. The context tells you whether an initiation is kind or cruel.
fact: Initiation is a noun, and the verb it comes from is initiate.
fact: «Initiation» can mean a ceremony or test that makes someone a new member of a group, club or team.
fact: «Initiation» can mean the start of a plan or process, as in «the initiation of talks».
fact: In science, initiation means the start of a reaction or process.
fact: Hazing is a cruel or dangerous initiation, and schools and clubs ban it.
exercise: «The new members took part in a secret initiation ceremony at the club.» What does initiation mean here? | A school lunch | A type of football kit | *A ceremony that makes you a new member | A holiday trip
exercise: «The leaders announced the initiation of talks about the new park.» What does initiation mean here? | *The start of the talks | The end of the talks | A quiet room for reading | A long argument
exercise: Which of these is a cruel, unsafe initiation that schools ban? | *Hazing | A welcome party with cake | A secret handshake | A club badge
test: «The teacher explained that the initiation of the reaction needs heat.» What does initiation mean here? | The cleaning up afterwards | The cooling down | *The start of the reaction | The end of the lesson
test: Initiation comes from a verb. Which word is that verb? | ceremony | initiation | *initiate | member
exam: Maya says initiation is just a party. Why is she wrong? | *Initiation can mean a ceremony that makes someone a new member, or the start of a process | Initiation means the end of something | Initiation only means a party, so she is right | Initiation is a type of food
